  "rawBulletin": "India Meteorological Department\n(Ministry of Earth Sciences)\nNATIONAL BULLETIN NO. 9 (BOB/10/2026)\nTIME OF ISSUE:2200 HOURS IST DATED:16.11.2026\nFROM: INDIA METEOROLOGICAL DEPARTMENT (FAX NO. 24643965/24699216/24623220)\nTO: CONTROL ROOM, NDM, MINISTRY OF HOME AFFAIRS (FAX.NO. 23093750)\nCONTROL ROOM NDMA (FAX.NO. 26701729)\nCABINET SECRETARIAT (FAX.NO.23012284, 23018638)\nPS TO HON\u2019BLE MINISTER FOR S & T AND EARTH SCIENCES (FAX NO.23316745)\nSECRETARY, MOES (FAX NO. 24629777)\nH.Q. (INTEGRATED DEFENCE STAFF AND CDS) (FAX NO. 23005137/23005147)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, DOORDARSHAN (23385843)\nDIRECTOR GENERAL, AIR (23421105, 23421219)\nPIB MOES (FAX NO. 23389042)\nUNI (FAX NO. 23355841)\nD.G. NATIONAL DISASTER RESPONSE FORCE (NDRF) (FAX NO. 26105912, 2436 3260)\nDIRECTOR, PUNCTUALITY, INDIAN RAILWAYS (FAX NO. 23388503)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDAMAN & NICOBAR ISLANDS (FAX NO. 03192-232656)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ANDHRA PRADESH (FAX NO. 0863-2441029)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF ODISHA (FAX NO. 0674-2536660)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT OF TELANGANA (FAX NO 040-23455340)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF TAMIL NADU (FAX NO. 044-25672304)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF PUDUCHERRY (FAX NO. 0413-2334145)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF CHHATTISGARH (FAX NO. 0771-2221206)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF JHARKHAND (FAX NO. 0651-2400255)\nCHIEF SECRETARY, GOVT. OF WEST BENGAL (FAX NO. 033-22144328)\nSub: Deep Depression intensified into Cyclonic Storm \u201cAkvan\u201d [Pronunciation: Akvan]\nover central parts of South and adjoining Westcentral Bay of Bengal [Cyclone Alert for\nAndhra Pradesh and adjoining South Odisha coasts\u2014Orange Message]\nThe Deep Depression over Southeast & adjoining Southwest Bay of Bengal moved north-\nnorthwestwards with the speed of 10 kmph during past 06 hours, intensified into a cyclonic storm\n\u201cAkvan\u201d [Pronunciation: Akvan]\u201d and lay centered at 1730 hours IST of today, the 16th\nNovember, 2026 over central parts of South and adjoining Westcentral Bay of Bengal, near\nLatitude 12.2\u00b0N and Longitude 85.7\u00b0E, about 610 km east of Chennai (Tamil Nadu), 630 km\nnortheast of Trincomalee (Sri Lanka), 660 km southeast of Machilipatnam (Andhra Pradesh), 670\nkm south-southeast of Visakhapatnam (Andhra Pradesh) and 790 km south of Gopalpur\n(Odisha).\nIt is very likely to continue to move north-northwestwards and intensify further into a Severe\nCyclonic Storm over westcentral Bay of Bengal around evening of 17th November, 2026.\nThereafter, it is likely to move northwestwards and intensify further into a very severe cyclonic\nstorm around 19th November morning.\nContinuing to move northwestward, it is likely to cross Andhra Pradesh & Yanam coasts between\nNellore and Tuni, around noon of 20th November, 2026 as a very severe cyclonic storm with the\nmaximum sustained wind speed of 120-130 kmph gusting to 145 kmph.\nForecast location and intensity are given in following table:\nDate/Time Position Maximum sustained surface Category of cyclonic\n(IST) (Lat. 0N/ long. 0E) wind speed (Kmph) disturbance\n16.11.26/1730 12.2/85.7 60-70 gusting to 80 Cyclonic Storm\n16.11.26/2330 12.7/85.3 65-75 gusting to 85 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/0530 13.1/84.8 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1130 13.4/84.3 80-90 gusting to 100 Cyclonic Storm\n17.11.26/1730 13.7/83.9 90-100 gusting to 110 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/0530 14.0/83.4 100-110 gusting to 120 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n18.11.26/1730 14.4/82.9 110-120 gusting to 130 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/0530 14.8/82.4 115-125 gusting to 140 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n19.11.26/1730 15.2/81.8 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/0530 15.5/81.3 120-130 gusting to 145 Very Severe Cyclonic Storm\n20.11.26/1730 15.9/80.8 110-120 gusting to 130 Severe Cyclonic Storm\n21.11.26/0530 16.3/80.3 70-80 gusting to 90 Cyclonic Storm\n21.11.26/1730 17.0/80.0 40-50 gusting 60 Depression\nWarnings:\n(i) Rainfall Warning:\nTamil Nadu, Puducherry & Karaikal: Light to moderate rainfall at many places with heavy rainfall at\nisolated places is very likely over No",
